f = "CORE-PR-HANDOFF-v13.md"
s = open(f, encoding="utf-8").read()
lines = s.split("\n")
def idx(p): return next(i for i, l in enumerate(lines) if l.startswith(p))
s_ = "\n".join(lines).replace("is accepted by the grant code (`raw-pg-m3-v13.txt`)", "is accepted by the grant code (`raw-pg-real-code-v13.txt`, check M3)")
lines = s_.split("\n")
lines[idx("**Questions for the lead")] = "**Questions for the lead (all non-blocking for the demo; L1 is gone; L9 is new in v13):**"
lines[idx("- **L4**")] = "- **L4** Resume core (yes), and the owner's answers D5 (below) and S-3. **Unbundled in v13:** D5 and S-3 are two separate owner questions; neither blocks S-1 (D5 is non-blocking, answer Q28; the design assumes option A)."
lines[idx("- **L5**")] = "- **L5** (needs-lead, answer needed before G-2) Q33 and Q34 say \"seven PRs\"; the other-tracks file lists nine. Offer: **confirm that all nine proceed** (each only after its own NEEDED-CHECK file exists) and L5 is closed; or name the two that are out."
lines[idx("- **L6**")] = lines[idx("- **L6**")] + " **If the zoom-out agent returns CANNOT-DECIDE** for a PR: that PR stays unbuilt, the lead may accept a checked file of an earlier probe as the evidence (a path and line numbers the agent read), and the file says so."
lines[idx("- **L7**")] = "- **L7** (needs-lead; silence rule) The extra clause of migration 0006: `usd >= 0 AND usd < 'Infinity'::numeric`. Q34 named only `usd >= 0`; without the second clause a not-a-number total passes the check (5.6 item 1). Run on 16.15: 16 checks, all refused (`raw-pg-b1-v13.txt`). **If you do not object by 2026-11-30 the clause stays in the held file; you can still refuse it at the move PR.** It is held outside `store/migrations/` and applied only on the owner's yes (runner gate `owner_gates.py`, 5.6)."
lines[idx("- **L8**")] = lines[idx("- **L8**")] + " **DB-1 and DB-2 together do not close it either:** DB-2 stops a key rewrite and records each lowering; it does not stop the lowering."
i = idx("- **L8**")
lines.insert(i + 1, "- **L9** (needs-lead, new in v13) **DB-2 needs its own yes from you.** DB-2 is the second held SQL file (a trigger that refuses a key change, and a table that records each lowering of a total; 5.6, `held-sql/spend_decrease_log.sql`). It is **not** part of Q34, which covers only the `CHECK` in DB-1. It adds a table and a trigger that cost about 0.28 ms per lowering and about 167 bytes per record (measured on 16.15, 5.6). Without your yes DB-2 is not built, and the key rewrite and the missing record of lowerings stay open (security major M1, labelled needs-lead).")
j = idx("**D5, the money unit")
lines[j] = ("**D5, the money unit of any NEW spend table: OWNER-OPEN, no default, non-blocking for the demo (answer Q28).** v10 said \"whole nano-dollars if nobody answers\"; that was a silent default on a money unit and is withdrawn (security review N8). The three options are in section 1 (Money type). **v13 assumes option A (decimal US dollars, as today) for the design, as a working assumption and not as the owner's answer.** What changes if the owner answers differently: for B the new spend table gets a `BIGINT` nano-dollar column, `add_spend` and `spend_totals` convert at the edge, `SpendWindow` and the status line are unchanged, DB-1's `CHECK` becomes `nano >= 0`, and DB-1 and DB-2 are rewritten before they are applied; for C every money value in `limits`, the stores and the demo meters changes and the PR series grows by a rename PR that must merge first. Merge order while D5 is open: S-1, S-2a and S-2b do not depend on the unit of a **database** column (they use the existing decimal columns), so they may merge; DB-1 and DB-2 are held and are not applied until D5 is answered or option A is accepted in writing (gate G-4). Exact question for the lead to put to the owner after the demo: \"For the money values of the new spend code, do you choose (A) decimal US dollars as today, as a written exception to the rule 'money is integers'; (B) whole nano-dollars for a new table only, two units side by side; or (C) integers everywhere, the largest change?\" Review-by 2026-12-31.")
open(f, "w", encoding="utf-8").write("\n".join(lines))
